# apps/checkout-pay/.env.stage — template (the real `.env.stage` is
# committed alongside since it carries no secrets — just a public URL).
#
# Vite reads this when invoked as `vite build --mode stage`. The
# VITE_-prefixed value below is statically replaced into the bundle at
# compile time and surfaces as `import.meta.env.VITE_BACKEND_URL` in
# `src/backend.ts`.
#
# Wave 4 P5 — the hosted-checkout buyer page is served from a separate
# subdomain (`pay-stage.muhaven.app`) so the kernel-passkey ceremony's
# RP-ID (`muhaven.app`) resolves correctly against the dashboard's
# apex. Without this env override, the bundle's hostname heuristic
# in `backend.ts:DEFAULT_BASE` already routes `pay-stage.muhaven.app`
# requests to `https://api-stage.muhaven.app` — this file is the
# explicit build-time pin for off-host deploy targets (e.g. preview
# environments or a separate Cloudflare Pages route).
VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://api-stage.muhaven.app
